WEBVTT

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
Hop, step, jump.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.140
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.950
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.400
Who I wanna be. {naritai atashi}

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.650
They call me calm, strong, and cool. {cool de tsuyoku...}

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.000
Everyone says I'm popular.{iketeru to...}

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.410
But the truth is, I'm not like that at all. {honto wa...}

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.620
I'm just an ordinary girl! {futsuu ni...}

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.730
I wish I could just get rid {puressha nank...}

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:54.510
of all this pressure and be myself. {sunao ni naritai...}

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.350
But they'd all say it's out of character. {kyarajanai toka...}

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.760
Unlock my heart! {atashi no kokoro...}

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:08.110
Just be who you wanna be. {naritai...}

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.960
Your Guardian Characters are with you. {shugo kyara ga...}

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.210
Just do it the way you wanna do it. {yaritai...}

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.280
It'll be okay, really! {zenzen...}

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:23.190
Just be who you wanna be. {naritai...}

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.960
Having only one style would be way too boring. {hitotsu...}

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.220
Just do it the way you wanna do it. {yaritai...}

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:34.490
You can do anything! {nandatte...}

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:36.110
I know that...{kitto}

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.950
Hop, step, jump.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.840
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.710
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.020
...is who I wanna be. {naritai atashi}

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:06.140
The quality of the dance has truly improved significantly.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.980
From a young age, that child has practiced harder than anyone else.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.520
Indeed, without missing a single day.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.270
Which is why the time has finally come.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.020
The time to set off on a journey.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.680
Nadeshiko! A Springtime Farewell!?

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.680
Episode 25

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:49.550
Bah.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:50.910
You need to train more.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.970
Sheesh, you're so undependable.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.470
Man...

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:55.750
One more try!

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.970
Please try your best, everyone.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.060
Yaya-chan.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.650
If you keep nodding off,

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.960
you're never going to finish.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.590
This paperwork's a pain. Can't we just do it tomorrow?

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.560
We cannot.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.310
We must finish it today.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:15.700
Jeez, Na-chin's a meanie!

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.020
Ha, you got in trouble!

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.910
Be quiet!

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:30.630
That won't do.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:33.050
You must do a proper cleaning job.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.930
But when the weather's this nice...

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:36.560
Huh?

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.140
What happened to Ran and Miki?

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.140
What nice weather.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.640
So warm and fuzzy.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:42.890
Jeez.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:44.270
Hinamori Amu!

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:45.700
Found ya!

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.470
Whoa, Misaki!

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:48.130
Hinamori-san!

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.520
And everyone else.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.740
Check this out.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.240
It's a matchmaking temple!

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.640
A matchmaking temple?

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.100
The matchmaking temple

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.220
is an ally to all girls who want their love to come true!

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.220
What are you looking at?

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.010
Oh, it's Amu-chi!

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.130
Amu-chi!

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.110
Hey!

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.810
The sunlight's become so soft.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.590
Yes.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:13.520
Spring is right around the corner.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.310
But, but...

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.560
Doesn't that mean Kukai's about to graduate?

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.230
What's this, Yaya?

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.380
You're not going to let me graduate?

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.830
Once we lose Soma-kun, our oldest member,

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.990
we'll have to work harder.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:28.660
Hotori-kun,

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.350
about that...

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:34.270
H-How dare you hang onto the King's back! {hey, this may be a 3-liner, but it seems to make sense to me like this}

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:35.430
Hold on, everyone.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:35.430
Hurry it up, then!

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.170
I have something I need to tell you.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.020
Is that true, Fujisaki-san?

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.570
It was decided a while ago.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.520
I just couldn't bring myself to tell you.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:52.350
It would've made you all gloomy if I did.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.890
Na-chin...

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.640
Don't look so sad.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.120
It's not as if we'll never see each other again.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.860
Does Hinamori-san know about this?

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:09.670
Amazing, right?

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:12.770
Matchmaking Temple

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:12.770
Stories of Personal Experiences

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:12.770
You just say a prayer, and your love's guaranteed to come true!

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.060
Please!

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:14.780
Huh?

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.430
Please match me up with Tadase-kun!

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:19.160
Hold on, Misaki.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.320
Didn't you give up on Tadase-kun and switch to Kukai?

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:23.990
That love is over!

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.630
I came back to Tadase-kun just recently!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:27.770
Unbelievable.

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:31.180
How can you change who you like so readily?

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.750
What about you, Hinamori Amu?

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.270
Who do you like right now?

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.770
Why don't you pray to the matchmaking temple god?

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.030
I want to know who Hinamori-san likes, too!

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:41.350
Huh?

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:42.520
Who is it?

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.560
Th-The person I like?

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.640
Th-That would have to be...

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:51.890
Please God...

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:54.730
Hello, Hinamori-san.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.720
Do you mind if I join you?

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:59.350
Ta-Tadase-kun!

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:01.470
Ikuto!

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:03.930
If you're gonna pray, stick with me.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.800
Don't bother with that little kid.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.220
Got it, Amu?

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.170
Hold it right there!

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:12.220
I'll be taking Hinamori!

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.220
Kukai!

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.780
Hello?

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.310
Whose face popped into your mind?

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.190
N-Nobody in particular.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.870
It's stupid to rely on gods.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:26.160
And I'm not interested in love or boys to begin with.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:27.680
See ya.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:31.420
That not surprising, coming from Hinamori Amu.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.800
"Cool & spicy!"

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.680
Jeez, what's wrong with me?

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:37.950
Seriously, this is the pits!

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:40.060
I'm supposed to be devoted to my prince!

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.680
Why did all those other faces pop up?

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:44.570
That means I'm totally unfaithful!

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.700
Something's wrong!

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:46.450
This is weird!

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:48.180
It's definitely not normal!

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.590
There, there, Amu-chan.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.310
Don't be so depressed about it.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:57.450
Who cares if you like a bunch of people?

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:01.280
A woman is defined by the number of loves she has.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:04.200
Don't put me on the same level as you!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:09.180
The one I like is Tadase-kun, isn't it?

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:12.180
But whenever I'm with Ikuto, my heart races.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.640
And Kukai can be pretty manly at times.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:18.520
What do I do?!

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:19.960
Okay!

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.590
I should turn to Nadeshiko in times like this.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.270
I'll go ask her.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.970
She's the one who understands my feelings best.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.480
Amu-tan and the others are going to be shocked when they hear about this.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:43.240
Still, why doesn't she tell Hinamori Amu about something so important?

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:45.520
Aren't they supposed to be best friends?

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:48.270
It's <i>because</i> they're best friends.

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:51.210
I understand how Na-chin feels.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:54.430
I don't wanna see Amu-chi look sad either!

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:55.470
Nadeshiko? {start is overlapping,}

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.180
Huh?

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.240
Where's Nadeshiko?

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:04.520
She's not here?

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.460
Fu-Fujisaki-san?

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.500
Sh-She had something to do, so she went home.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.390
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:11.800
Went home?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:12.730
Jeez, Nadeshiko!

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:14.850
Why'd you have to run off at such a critical time?

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:17.610
How dare you leave me all alone, you heartless meanie!

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.070
What's wrong?

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.410
N-Nothing! Nothing at all!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.480
Why are you avoiding my eyes?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.090
W-We're not doing anything like that.

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:27.020
Right?

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.420
Y-Yeah!

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:29.720
You're hiding something.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.330
Something's definitely funny here!

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:34.330
And that's upside-down!

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:40.680
Forget it.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:42.060
Let's go.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:53.570
I kind of came here on the spur of the moment.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:54.830
It's Nadeshiko's house!

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:56.350
We haven't been here in a while.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:58.460
Still, every time I see this...

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:00.510
The pressure of history and tradition...

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.060
It's a little intimidating.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.520
But I can't leave my feelings like this!

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.050
I'm sure if I talk to Nadeshiko...

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:08.730
Your heart will be at peace.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.390
You'll be able to sort out your feelings.

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:12.040
You'll be able to sigh in relief.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:12.770
Exactly.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.770
Young Master!

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:18.060
Young Master Nagihiko!

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:19.930
Nagihiko?

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.610
Where did he go?

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:24.680
The others have all assembled.

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:27.440
H-Hello.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:28.900
M-Miss Hinamori...

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.360
I haven't seen you in a while.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:31.960
Um, who's this "Young Master?"

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.180
W-Well, that would be...

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:34.950
You rang?

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:44.220
I'm right here.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.570
Nadeshiko?

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:50.470
It's not.

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.810
He looks just like Nadeshiko.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.920
But he's a boy?

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.570
Hello, Amu-chan.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.060
Did you come to see Nadeshiko?

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.320
Uh-huh.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:02.230
Um, how did you know my name?

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:03.180
Young Master!

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.750
Everyone is waiting!

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:05.470
Oops.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:07.370
Huh?

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.060
We're running for it!

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.600
Young Master!

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.470
H-Hold on!

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:22.560
Sorry, was I going too fast?

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.800
No. But what's going on?

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:25.700
Who are you?

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.310
You look just like Nadeshiko.

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:29.140
I'm Nagihiko.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.020
Nadeshiko's twin brother.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:32.410
Twin?

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:33.540
Twins.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.350
Twins.

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:37.720
Twins?!

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.620
Yep, twins.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.280
Normally, we live apart.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.220
But I've just returned today.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:47.020
All of our relatives have gathered for a certain reason.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.660
Don't you need to go back to the house?

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:50.850
It's okay.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:53.270
Besides, I wanted to talk with you, Amu-chan.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.350
Nadeshiko is always talking about you.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.400
She says you're her best friend.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:59.520
Best friend...

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.810
That has a nice ring to it.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.370
Come on, let's go!

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.080
It'd be a waste to just stand around.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:04.690
Huh?

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:05.390
Go where?

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.600
The matchmaking temple.

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:28.940
Nagihiko.

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:33.120
I had no idea Nadeshiko had an older twin brother.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.830
But they really do look the same.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:39.950
Over here.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:40.600
It's a shortcut.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:42.350
Ah, okay.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:52.180
This is my secret way out.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.140
Secret way out?

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:56.770
Um, Nagihiko...

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:59.780
You're still holding my hand.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.620
Oh, you're right.

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.140
It's different today.

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:04.660
Today?

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.450
Nagihiko.

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.270
What a mysterious boy.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:13.140
He kind of makes me wonder...

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:18.030
Nagi's pretty good at dealing with Amu-chan.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:19.880
He's cool.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.560
That's one heck of a playboy.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:39.100
I had no idea there was such a pretty park out here.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:41.810
Wh-What?

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:43.270
Did I do something?

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:45.530
Benkei, it's me! It's me!

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:48.550
There, there.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:49.830
That tickles!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.970
Young Master.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.720
Young Master Nagihiko.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.360
Wait one minute.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:00.160
Huh?

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:11.530
Here.

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:13.210
Thanks!

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:14.470
You're welcome.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.140
He's just like Nadeshiko;

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:18.770
a genius at calming everyone down!

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.520
They really are twins.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.260
I haven't seen you in a long time, Young Master.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:26.270
Are you on a date with this cute young lady today?

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:27.810
D-Date?

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:30.740
No, I just met Nagihiko for the first time today.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.300
So, um...

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.070
That's right.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:33.920
Huh?

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.020
She's a lively young lady.

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:45.160
Please help yourselves.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:46.220
Thank you.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:52.730
Are you familiar with this area, Nagihiko?

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:57.500
When I was little, I used to sneak out of training and explore around here.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.380
Was Nadeshiko with you?

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:00.220
Uh-huh.

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:03.500
The training must have been tough.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:04.810
True.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:07.960
But I never thought of it as something painful.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:10.710
When I dance, I completely assume that role.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:13.770
It's fun to be able to express the feelings of many different people.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:16.230
I want to put on a better performance.

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:18.890
I've always felt that way.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:22.510
Both you and Nadeshiko are really responsible people.

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:26.110
And then there's me...

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:27.930
Is something on your mind?

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.010
Yeah.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:32.060
I was going to talk to Nadeshiko about it.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:37.010
Can you talk to me about it instead?

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:41.880
Not a chance!

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:44.520
How fickle am I, seriously?

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:49.800
I see.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:51.820
You're only supposed to like one person,

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.350
yet you think about a number of different boys,

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:55.830
and that bothers you.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.430
Uh-huh.

00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:02.470
Why am I telling Nagihiko these things when we just met?

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:05.500
Maybe it's easy to talk to him because he looks like Nadeshiko?

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:07.640
We're here.

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:09.010
Huh?

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.600
Ah, this is...

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.870
The matchmaking temple.

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:14.470
Let's pay it a visit.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:17.770
Amu-chan?

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:20.450
I think I'll pass.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:20.970
Huh?

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.800
If I go in with my feelings so jumbled,

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:26.470
I'll make the matchmaking god angry.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:34.870
At what point does like become love?

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:35.580
Huh?

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:38.260
You like your friends.

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:40.100
You like people you admire.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:41.850
There are different kinds of like, agreed?

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:48.600
I wonder where you draw the boundary between like and true love.

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:54.470
Amu-chan, what do you like about the prince?

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:55.170
Huh?

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:56.940
Wh-When I first transferred here,

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:59.450
I saw him at a Guardians' assembly,

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:01.440
and I thought he looked cool.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.580
And then...

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:06.820
I see.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:10.650
So you didn't know the real prince when you started liking him.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:11.100
Huh?

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.490
The real prince?

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:26.010
I didn't know anything about the real Tadase-kun,

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:28.980
until I became a Guardian.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:31.310
I only saw his outside character.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:34.750
People tend to make judgments based on appearances.

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:38.710
But a person's real self

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.890
may turn out to be completely different from his appearance.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:51.840
That's true.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:55.680
There are still so many things I don't know.

00:16:56.100 --> 00:16:57.470
About everybody else.

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:59.160
About my own feelings.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:01.770
I'm still a fledgling at love.

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:03.470
No, I'm just an egg.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:07.200
For now, I want to learn as much as I can.

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:08.500
About my friends.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:09.880
About myself.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.030
About what it means to like someone.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:13.750
As much as I can.

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:22.800
Here.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.390
It's a matchmaking charm.

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.010
Thanks.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:27.310
It's the same as mine.

00:17:27.590 --> 00:17:28.610
Same?

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:31.650
Did you pray to be matched with someone, too?

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:34.830
No one at the moment.

00:17:35.310 --> 00:17:36.810
Since I'm still in training.

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:38.220
What's with that?

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:41.600
You sounded like this big love expert a minute ago!

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:44.440
Girls are complicated.

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:46.500
I still have much to learn.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.520
But there <i>is</i> a girl I'm concerned about.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:51.680
Huh?

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:56.350
Due to certain circumstances, I can't show her my true self right now.

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:59.520
But until the day I can reveal my true self...

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:03.070
Until that day comes, I'll watch over her.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:07.280
Even if we end up far apart.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:22.440
Nagihiko, huh?

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:24.930
He's a pretty mysterious boy.

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:27.430
We ended up not running into Nadeshiko,

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:29.870
but you still seem pretty satisfied.

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:34.180
Amu-chan's mind is stuck on Nagihiko now!

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:34.820
Huh?

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:36.370
Th-That's not true!

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:40.520
But you completely forgot about us, didn't you?

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:41.220
{giku? some sound effect reacting to previous line}

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.560
That's our Amu-chan!

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:44.370
A grade-schooler with a lot of loves!

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:46.450
A devil of a woman!

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:49.740
Though, you could just say that she's easily swayed.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:50.780
Hey!

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:53.490
I let you speak your minds and you all go nuts!

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:55.110
She's mad! She's mad!

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.260
I'm home.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.140
Young Master Nagihiko!

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:01.700
Ah, what a relief.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:02.930
Hurry up and get ready!

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:04.930
Sorry, Baya.

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:08.200
Everyone is waiting for your final dance, Young Master,

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:11.180
since you'll be leaving Japan tomorrow.

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.000
Isn't that a fine thing?

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.490
Madam!

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:18.330
Boys should be active that way.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.070
Welcome back.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:30.000
The men of the Fujisaki line

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.270
must dress as females when they are children,

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:34.720
and live with a female name.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:38.520
All for the sake of learning female dance,

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:39.870
according to the Fujisaki family way.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:45.850
That being said, he'll probably suffocate if he isn't allowed to go back to being a boy every once in a while.

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:52.290
Besides, I'm sure he wanted to make some memories with that girl before he left on his long journey.

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:57.680
Your hairpin is crooked, Nadeshiko.

00:19:57.680 --> 00:19:58.680
There.

00:19:58.680 --> 00:19:59.940
Thank you.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.990
Shall we go?

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:10.310
Yes.

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.770
Is that true?

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:22.170
Uh-huh.

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:26.040
Fujisaki-san is going to study in Europe.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.930
She wants to expand her repertoire

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:31.010
by studying the traditional dances of other countries.

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:33.640
Her plane's probably taken off already.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:36.520
Without even saying good-bye?

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:40.890
Here, Hinamori-san.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:40.910
To Amu-chan

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:42.510
It's from Fujisaki-san.

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:52.890
Amu-chan, sorry this happened so suddenly.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:56.990
I plan to return in a year after improving my dancing.

00:20:57.470 --> 00:21:01.880
When that happens, you'll be surprised by how I look when we meet again.

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:03.640
So look forward to it.

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:08.050
I don't want to say good-bye to you.

00:21:08.050 --> 00:21:11.180
So instead, I'll say...

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:13.890
Thank you.

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:26.600
Hinamori-san!

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:26.600
Amu-chi!

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:28.310
Amu-chan!

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:53.140
You have to!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.680
You have to come back!

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:09.780
You have to.

00:22:10.270 --> 00:22:12.140
Because you promised.

00:22:13.030 --> 00:22:14.290
Right, Nadeshiko?

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:41.390
Unless the world ends, I'll always {sekai ga...}

00:22:41.390 --> 00:22:44.160
love you!  Yeah, you! {suki da yo...}

00:22:44.160 --> 00:22:47.630
'Cause I just love, love, love you! {suki suki suki...}

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:52.360
Sure, I might struggle, but I'm still living. {jitabata...}

00:22:52.360 --> 00:22:55.040
So figure it out already! Yeah, you! {kizukeyo...}

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:58.680
Even though I love, love, love you, {suki suki suki...}

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:04.870
I wanna say it but, shoot, I just can't! {iitaikuseni...}

00:23:04.870 --> 00:23:08.990
I wanna show you what's in my heart! {tsutaetai...}

00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:12.420
Oh yes! You're my one true hero. {oh yes!...}

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:17.580
Being in love's gonna be a bumpy ride.  {koishiterukagiri...}

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:23.510
But keep going! Okay, greenhorn rider? {hashitsuzukero...}

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:28.760
Straight down the path, into the sunset, stronger and stronger. {yuuyake...}

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:37.630
Ride through the wild land of youth. {seishun no...}

00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:53.090
Nadeshiko's gone far away.

00:23:53.090 --> 00:23:54.700
Don't be so down!

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:56.280
Amu-chan's spaced out.

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:57.870
It's so lonely.

00:23:57.870 --> 00:23:59.370
It can't be helped.

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:01.050
Spring is said to be the season of farewells.

00:24:01.050 --> 00:24:02.220
Um, w-wait.

00:24:02.220 --> 00:24:03.060
Kukai, too?

00:24:03.060 --> 00:24:03.490
Yep.

00:24:03.490 --> 00:24:05.060
Since I'm graduating.

00:24:05.060 --> 00:24:06.510
I'll be in middle school this spring.

00:24:06.510 --> 00:24:09.550
I-I forgot!

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:10.910
Next time on Shugo Chara:

00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:12.330
A New Beginning!

00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:13.450
Don't cry, Hinamori!

00:24:13.450 --> 00:24:15.650
Do your best every day so you have no regrets!

00:24:15.650 --> 00:24:16.380
That's the basic rule!

00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:18.940
I hate spring!
